      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In four patients hospitalized with severe neuralgic complaints in conjunction with a Zoster infection, the pain-relieving effect of oral 1-adamantanamine sulfate used in combination with carbamazepine was studied. From the results obtained, the oral administration of 1-adamantanamine sulfate also appears to have a reliable analgesic effect, so that ambulatory treatment is readily possible."},
